flowchart TB
%% Five independent controls. That they are independent is the point, and it is why they are
%% drawn as five stacked boxes with no arrows between them rather than as a chain: any one of
%% them being wrong has to leave the other four standing. A single gate that "mostly works" is
%% one bug away from nothing; five narrow ones are one bug away from four.
%%
%% The invisible links exist only to force one box per row.

  rbac["1. RBAC<br/>get, list, watch — no write verb anywhere.<br/>No secrets, no pods/exec, no token minting."] ~~~ netpol
  netpol["2. Network policy<br/>default-deny both directions.<br/>Egress is a short written list."] ~~~ admission
  admission["3. Admission<br/>Kyverno policies on the agent's own identity,<br/>so a merged pull request cannot widen it."] ~~~ secrets
  secrets["4. Secrets<br/>one path in, from a vault.<br/>The agent has no path to any value."] ~~~ prgate
  prgate["5. The pull request<br/>a human merges everything,<br/>with a different identity to the author."]

  note["Every one of these is a file in git, so widening the first four is a diff somebody reads."]

  prgate -.-> note

  classDef control fill:#121820,stroke:#71b7ff,stroke-width:2px,color:#e7edf3
  class rbac,netpol,admission,secrets,prgate control
